# React Native (Expo) map — generated for {{ public }}

The files here are pre-wired to your server (`src/config.js`). Because Expo/React Native
versions move quickly, we do not pin them — create a fresh project and drop these files in:

```bash
npx create-expo-app@latest {{ project }}-map --template blank
cd {{ project }}-map
npx expo install react-native-webview react-native-safe-area-context
# copy App.js and src/ from this folder over the new project, then:
npx expo start
```

* `App.js` — bilingual (KA/EN) wrapper around your server's web map. Works in Expo Go,
  no API keys.
* `src/MapLibreScreen.js` — optional fully native, open-source map (MapLibre) with a layer
  switcher. Needs a development build; see the header comment in that file.

{% if tls == 'none' %}
**Plain HTTP:** Android blocks cleartext traffic in release builds. Either enable HTTPS in the
installer or set `"android": {"usesCleartextTraffic": true}` via `expo-build-properties`.
{% endif %}
